@preamble let signal = import("signal")
watch
@unchecked
Subscribes to one or more portable signal names and returns a receive-only Aiki channel. Received values are signal symbols and can participate in recv or select. Supported signal names may vary by substrate; unsupported names return a shaped :unsupported error.

watch(...signals)
===
stop
@unchecked
Stops delivery to a channel returned by signal.watch. Repeated host signal delivery may coalesce; signals are event notifications rather than a lossless message queue.

stop(source)
===
send
@unchecked
Sends a portable signal to a process handle. The substrate maps the semantic signal where it can do so faithfully; unsupported signal/host combinations return a shaped :unsupported error.

send(process, signal)
